WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.467
-Longtime Trump ally
Chris Christie is

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:05.167
on a media rehabilitation tour,

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.968
ahead of a possible run
for president in 2024,

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.767
while the man he helped
catapult into office

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.734
is still spreading
the same unhinged lies

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:13.267
about the election, this time,

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:14.667
and an interview
with Mike Lindell.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.634
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:21.067
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:24.000
If you've been watching CNN
or MSNBC lately,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.133
it seems like there's been
one person, in particular,

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.200
who's been more ubiquitous
than ever.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.767
-We've spent the past hour

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:30.968
on Chris Christie

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:33.234
and what it's like to be him.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.667
-Still ahead on "Morning Joe,"

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.267
former New Jersey
Governor Chris Christie.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.834
-Former governor of New Jersey
Chris Christie

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.801
will join the conversation.
-When we come back,

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:42.400
Chris Christie.
-Joining us now,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.000
former New Jersey Governor
Chris Christie.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.801
-Joining us now,
the aforementioned

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.400
Chris Christie.
-We're back with former

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.734
New Jersey Governor
Chris Christie.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.467
-Chris Christie joins me now.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:53.133
-Former Republican governor
of New Jersey
Chris Christie.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.200
-I mean, at this point,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.300
Christie's on cable news
so much,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.467
they're going
to start putting him

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.200
in a tiny box
in the corner of the screen.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.434
[ Laughter ]
"And let's check in

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:00.634
on our Christie Cam.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.968
[ Laughter ]
Oh! Looks like he's arguing

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.467
with a stagehand about the Jets.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:05.701
Let's see how this plays out."

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.234
[ Laughter ]
I mean, my God,

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:08.767
he's been on cable news
more often than

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.067
the reverse mortgage commercials
starring Tom Selleck.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.400
[ Laughter ]
At least do us the courtesy

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.000
of growing the mustache,
Christie!

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.534
[ Laughter ]
Also, damn you, Selleck,
and your silver tongue!

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:18.801
[ Laughter ]
I took out a reverse mortgage,

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.200
thinking I'd score
some quick cash,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.901
and, now, Tom Selleck lives
in my house

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.000
with my wife and kids!

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.267
[ Laughter ]
In fact, he's doing

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.234
the reverse mortgage commercials
from my attic!

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:27.701
[ Laughter ]
And, even worse,

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.601
he's best friends
with the Sea Captain now.

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:30.868
[ Laughter ]
-Love me some Selleck.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.300
He's my favorite of the
"Three Men and a Baby."

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.767
Sorry, Guttenberg.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.334
[ Laughter ]
True story --

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.934
every night, I do a Q&amp;A
with the audience,

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.434
and, every night,
at least one person says,

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:40.534
"Bring back the Sea Captain,"

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:41.767
and then, the rest
of the audience

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.801
just starts chucking rocks
at whoever said it.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.767
[ Laughter ]
Meanwhile, all I can think is,

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.767
"Where did everybody get
loose rocks in New York?"

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:48.968
[ Laughter ]
Anyway...

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:51.234
[ Ding ]
...cable is so desperate
to fill time

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.901
that CNN even aired a ludicrous
special focused entirely

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.467
on Christie, called...

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.133
Is it called that
because "Being" is

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.701
the only title he has left?

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:01.634
[ Laughter ]
Governor? No, he left office

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.834
with a dismal approval rating.
Candidate? Oh, no.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.734
He crashed and burned hard
in the GOP primary.

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:08.367
But, he is still,
technically, a being.

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:09.968
[ Laughter ]
And I'm sorry,

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.234
but is there a mystery
to being Chris Christie?

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:13.567
You guys are acting like
he's some

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:15.467
weird-lifestyle-having guy

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.033
like everybody wants
to know about.

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:18.834
He's not Harry Styles or Banksy.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.300
He's a loudmouth
from New Jersey.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.534
If you want to know
what he's thinking,

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:22.601
you don't need CNN.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:23.968
You just have to be
within earshot,

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:25.667
[ Laughter ]
which is for him, I think,

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:27.200
like a mile?

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.901
[ Laughter ]
In fact, if this show
was authentic New Jersey,

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.434
it wouldn't be called
"Being Chris Christie."

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.334
It'd be called...

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:34.834
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:36.434
The only way I'd be interested

00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:38.100
in a show called
"Being Chris Christie" is

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.567
if I could enter his head,
"Being John Malkovich"-style,

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.033
and make him do something
embarrassing, like,

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.667
I don't know, stand
behind someone who hates him.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:44.734
Oh, right, you know,
he did that.

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:46.267
[ Laughter ]
Okay, I'd make him

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.234
sit alone on a closed beach.
Oh, he did that, too.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.434
[ Laughter ]
You know what? Never mind.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:51.267
Now, let's just establish,
right off the bat,

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:54.100
that Chris Christie is
without credibility,
when it comes to Trump.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.300
He repeatedly said he wasn't
suited to be president,

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.634
that he didn't have
the temperament

00:02:57.634 --> 00:02:59.300
or experience for the job.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.534
Then, he became one of the first
prominent Republicans

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.200
to endorse him in 2016.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.701
Then, he stood by him
throughout his presidency

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:08.467
and even helped him prep
for that first debate in 2020,

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:11.133
where Trump yelled nonstop
for 90 minutes,

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:12.834
like a caller
on a sports radio show

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.567
who shouts over Mike Francesa.

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:15.667
[ New Jersey accent ]
No, no, Mike,
you don't understand.

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:17.267
Excuse me, Mike.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:18.834
It's good that the Mets
let Syndergaard go.

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:22.334
Excuse me because Jacob deGrom
is never injured.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.968
[ Laughter ]
You know, it's nice,
when the Mets are in the news,

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:25.567
to [bleep]
so we can take a break

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.367
from making fun of the Jets,
but it is true --

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:30.667
Noah Syndergaard, who was here,
on this show, not too long ago,

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.200
is now a Los Angeles Angel.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.400
And, when he was here,
he certainly acted

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.100
like he was going to be
a Met for life.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.901
There were some signs,
like, when I said,

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:38.901
"Hey, maybe we can get dinner
when the season starts,"

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:41.267
he said, "U..."

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:47.100
[ Laughter ]
...m...

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.167
maybe?"

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:50.767
So, your nickname
might be Thor, but to me,

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:51.767
you're a Loki.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.534
[ Laughter ]
[ Ding ]

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:54.968
Christie was so deeply invested

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.300
in getting Trump
elected president
and keeping him in office

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.801
that he helped prep him
for that [bleep]show debate,

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:01.567
where Trump was so insane
and unhinged

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.067
that the moderator had to keep
shouting the word no at him

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.868
like a dog who wouldn't stop
humping his owner's leg.

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:09.100
-I'll ask Joe. The individual --
-No.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.901
-Did you get a half million?
-No! Hey, Mr. President.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:12.267
-Which was heavily --
-No. Mr. President.

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:13.767
No, no, go ahead.
No, no, no.

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:15.968
Mr. President. Mr. President.
-$3.5 million, Joe.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.067
$3.5 million.
-No, no, no.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:18.100
No, Mr. President.
-Go ahead.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.400
-No!
-Can I be honest?

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.667
It's a very important question.
-Try to be honest.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:21.934
-No.
-It'd be good for you.
-He stood up.

00:04:21.934 --> 00:04:23.200
[ Laughter ]
He stood up
-No. The answer

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.467
to the question is no.
-and he threatened --

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.167
[ Laughter ]
-I mean, the only way

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.334
I want to hear from Christie is
if he told us

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.534
he was a double agent trying

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.601
to destroy Trump's campaign
from the inside.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.000
[ As Christie ]
Yeah, I helped him prep
for the debate,

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.367
told him issues were for losers

00:04:34.367 --> 00:04:36.400
and made him snort
half a dozen Pixy Stix.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.200
[ Laughter ]
But Christie was a key part
of the debate prep.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.501
In fact,
according to a new book...

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:46.033
[ Laughter ]
First of all, there's never been
a worse casting choice

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.834
[ Laughter ]
for the role of Joe Biden
than Chris Christie.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:50.033
Biden's a soft-talking grandpa
from Delaware,

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:51.567
and Christie's
a New Jersey bully

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.067
with the temperament
of a seagull

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:55.501
attacking a beach blanket
in Atlantic City.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.000
It's like if they couldn't
get Tom Hanks

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.701
to play Sully Sullenberger
and, instead,

00:04:58.701 --> 00:04:59.968
went with Al Pacino.

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:02.200
[ As Pacino ]
Whoa, buckle up, muchacho!

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.901
We are going down!

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:07.200
[ Laughter ]
We got hit by a loose goose.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:12.300
This is your captain, Sully.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.167
Isn't it weird?

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.300
If you had the last name
Sullenberger,

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.100
would you name your kid Sully?

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.534
[ Laughter ]
It's a nickname?

00:05:20.534 --> 00:05:22.467
What's his real --
Chesley?!

00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:24.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.567
But the reason Trump
apparently blew up at Christie

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:33.667
during that debate prep session
was because Trump was obsessed

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.534
with all the nonsense
conspiracy theories

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.934
Rudy Giuliani was pushing
about Biden and his family.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:40.534
So, Christie,
playing the part of Biden,

00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:42.667
brought up Trump's own
conflicts of interest

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.334
to prep him
for Biden's response.

00:05:57.567 --> 00:05:58.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.567
At one point,
Trump said to Christie...

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:08.567
I'm not going to sit here
and put up with it.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.300
Alright, first of all,
I love that,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.934
while they were trying
to prepare the president

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:13.467
for a nationally
televised debate,

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:15.234
Rudy was sitting there
distracting everyone,

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:16.701
trying to get his iPad to work.

00:06:16.701 --> 00:06:18.968
[ Laughter ]
[ As Giuliani ]
My iPad keeps freezing.

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:21.400
"Rudy, that's not an iPad.
That's a picture frame."

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.267
[ Laughter ]
[ As Giuliani ]
That can't be right.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:25.133
I got it from my IT guy,
Michael.

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:28.000
[ Laughter ]
Now, as you may know,

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.434
not only was that debate prep
a disaster,

00:06:30.434 --> 00:06:32.968
just in terms of the debate
itself, but, on top of that,

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.601
Christie and a bunch
of other people in the room

00:06:35.601 --> 00:06:37.767
got COVID from it
and, even then,

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:39.868
Trump apparently had no concern,
whatsoever,

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:40.934
for Christie's well-being.

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:42.133
In fact, in his new book...

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:49.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.234 --> 00:06:56.234
[ Laughter ]
He's talking about COVID

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:57.868
like Christie's RA just found

00:06:57.868 --> 00:06:59.501
a bag of weed
in his sock drawer.

00:06:59.501 --> 00:07:00.801
[ Laughter ]
[ As Trump ] Are you gonna say

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:02.501
you got it from me, Chris?
Because I'm already

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.000
on thin ice with the dean.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.400
[ Laughter ]
And, yet, despite the fact

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.701
that debate prep was a disaster
and he got yelled at by Trump

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:12.501
and that he was complicit in
and actively supportive of

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:14.400
a catastrophic
and deeply corrupt presidency

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.968
that, among other things,
subverted our democracy,

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:20.000
let a deadly respiratory disease
spiral wildly out of control,

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.434
and cratered our economy,
Christie said he really

00:07:22.434 --> 00:07:25.834
only had one regret
about his participation.

00:07:25.834 --> 00:07:27.901
-In the last days
of the Trump administration,

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:30.501
The New Yorker published a Q&amp;A
with you,

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:33.667
with the headline
"Chris Christie Has No Regrets."

00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:35.601
Really?
-I really don't.

00:07:35.601 --> 00:07:37.834
Look, Mike --
-You don't regret

00:07:37.834 --> 00:07:40.734
prepping Donald Trump
for his bid

00:07:40.734 --> 00:07:41.834
to run for reelection?

00:07:41.834 --> 00:07:43.901
-I do not.
I do not.

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:45.334
The only regret I have
about that is that --
-Some people --

00:07:45.334 --> 00:07:46.367
-The only regret I have
about that is

00:07:46.367 --> 00:07:48.234
I caught COVID
when I was doing it.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:49.567
[ Laughter ]
-It's pretty great
when you're trying to see

00:07:49.567 --> 00:07:51.601
if a person has
a guilty conscience

00:07:51.601 --> 00:07:52.868
and their only regret is --

00:07:52.868 --> 00:07:54.334
[ As Christie ] I got sick.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.334 --> 00:07:56.133
It's like a judge
asking a drunk driver

00:07:56.133 --> 00:07:58.634
if he has anything to say
before sentencing and they yell,

00:07:58.634 --> 00:07:59.767
"Just that no one seems to care

00:07:59.767 --> 00:08:01.734
that my Camaro's
all scratched up!"

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:03.100
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.267
So, now, Christie's trying

00:08:04.267 --> 00:08:06.300
to rehab his image
as part of a book tour,

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.667
by casting himself as some sort
of straight shooter,

00:08:08.667 --> 00:08:10.133
when it comes
to the 2020 election.

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:11.667
Look, I guess, at this point,

00:08:11.667 --> 00:08:13.033
any Republican
who's willing to say

00:08:13.033 --> 00:08:16.667
the election wasn't stolen
deserves a shred of credit,

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:18.434
which tells you just how far
the GOP has fallen.

00:08:18.434 --> 00:08:20.534
But, why are we taking
Chris Christie,

00:08:20.534 --> 00:08:22.100
of all people, seriously?
He stood by

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:24.200
this obviously monstrous man
for years

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:25.601
and he still refuses to say

00:08:25.601 --> 00:08:27.634
whether he'd support Trump again
in 2024.

00:08:27.634 --> 00:08:28.934
-Donald Trump has made it
pretty clear

00:08:28.934 --> 00:08:31.267
he wants to run
for president again.

00:08:31.267 --> 00:08:32.334
Would you support him?

00:08:33.968 --> 00:08:36.634
-Oh, look, I don't know
that he's going to run.

00:08:36.634 --> 00:08:38.501
-What if he does.
-I don't know
if I'm going to run.

00:08:38.501 --> 00:08:40.300
Oh, look, "What if?"

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.767
I've learned --
-I mean, it's not as if

00:08:41.767 --> 00:08:44.601
it's a big secret that he's
seriously considering it.

00:08:44.601 --> 00:08:46.300
-He's seriously considering it.
Let's see what happens

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.467
when he does
and let's see who he is

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:50.734
and what he says
and how he conducts himself.

00:08:50.734 --> 00:08:52.934
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yes, let's see
which Donald Trump will show up.

00:08:52.934 --> 00:08:55.300
Will it be the well-spoken
and serious statesman,

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.167
or will it be the one
who exists?

00:08:57.167 --> 00:08:58.467
[ Laughter and applause ]
You know,

00:08:58.467 --> 00:09:01.267
the being Donald Trump.

00:09:01.267 --> 00:09:03.033
I'm sorry, you still think
there's a mystery

00:09:03.033 --> 00:09:05.000
as to how Donald Trump
is going to conduct himself?

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.567
Having kids,
I've read a lot of books

00:09:06.567 --> 00:09:08.567
about what to expect
at different stages,

00:09:08.567 --> 00:09:09.734
but not one of them has said...

00:09:13.567 --> 00:09:15.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:16.968
It's especially ludicrous
to claim you don't know

00:09:16.968 --> 00:09:19.667
how Trump will conduct himself
when, as we speak,

00:09:19.667 --> 00:09:20.901
he's still spreading the big lie

00:09:20.901 --> 00:09:23.501
that Christie supposedly
criticizes him for.

00:09:23.501 --> 00:09:26.634
Trump just did an interview
with MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell,

00:09:26.634 --> 00:09:29.434
where he and Lindell competed
for worst posture

00:09:29.434 --> 00:09:31.634
[ Laughter ]
and rambled on
about the same old

00:09:31.634 --> 00:09:32.767
election conspiracy theories.

00:09:32.767 --> 00:09:34.267
And, by the way,
Christie has no credibility,

00:09:34.267 --> 00:09:35.734
especially when it comes
to questions

00:09:35.734 --> 00:09:38.334
about the 2020 election
because he repeatedly insisted,

00:09:38.334 --> 00:09:39.467
in the run-up to the election,

00:09:39.467 --> 00:09:41.100
that Trump would
accept the result,

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:43.834
even though Trump was loudly
proclaiming, at the time,

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:46.367
that the only way he could lose
is if it was stolen.

00:09:46.367 --> 00:09:48.200
-You know this guy well.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.067
Do you believe he would

00:09:51.067 --> 00:09:54.133
follow critical conventions
in the United States

00:09:54.133 --> 00:09:56.234
and have a peaceful transition
of power

00:09:56.234 --> 00:09:58.901
for those months
between this election result

00:09:58.901 --> 00:10:01.300
and the next inauguration?

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.434
-There's no question in my mind
that President Trump

00:10:04.434 --> 00:10:07.400
will participate in a peaceful
transition of power,

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.767
if he does not win
tomorrow night.

00:10:09.767 --> 00:10:11.434
-If it doesn't go
the president's way --

00:10:11.434 --> 00:10:12.834
you know him pretty well --

00:10:12.834 --> 00:10:14.701
is he prepared to accept defeat?

00:10:14.701 --> 00:10:16.834
-Yes.
Yeah, I think he is.

00:10:16.834 --> 00:10:19.734
I think there also is part
of him that knows

00:10:19.734 --> 00:10:22.467
that not leaving
the White House,

00:10:22.467 --> 00:10:26.434
putting up that kind of stink,
in terms of peaceful transition,

00:10:26.434 --> 00:10:28.200
just is not the way
he wants to leave.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.200
-I'm sorry, you thought Trump
wouldn't put up a stink?

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.968
That's all he ever does,
put up a stink.

00:10:31.968 --> 00:10:33.634
If he had his own line
of deodorant,

00:10:33.634 --> 00:10:34.968
that would be the tagline.

00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:36.067
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.067 --> 00:10:37.300
For the life of me,
I can't understand

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:38.934
why the media
is willingly participating

00:10:38.934 --> 00:10:41.200
in the rehabilitation
of a guy like Chris Christie.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.767
He was a central figure
in the rise

00:10:42.767 --> 00:10:44.501
of an obviously
horrendous president

00:10:44.501 --> 00:10:45.701
who left the nation in ruins.

00:10:45.701 --> 00:10:47.801
He shouldn't get a chance
to launder his reputation

00:10:47.801 --> 00:10:49.400
ahead of another
presidential run,

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:50.767
with reporters
following him around,

00:10:50.767 --> 00:10:52.601
asking him what he thinks.
The only two things that

00:10:52.601 --> 00:10:55.234
should follow Christie around
are support for Trump and...

00:10:55.234 --> 00:10:56.434
-A stink.

00:10:56.434 --> 00:10:59.501
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:59.501 --> 00:11:03.634
♪♪

